  "review_method": "Every rendered page was viewed as an image (the pdftoppm PNGs, opened one by one). The first full render (104 pages) was viewed in full; it showed the O1b row of the obligations table (page 8) saying that no Round33 gate addresses the obligation, where the record says that none closes it, table captions set directly on the top rule of the tables below them (for example Table 29, page 93), and a one-word line at the top of page 75 (the end of the paragraph that introduces the BC2 node display). The O1b wording was corrected (only page image 8 changed, SHA-256 comparison, and it was viewed again); a caption skip of 6pt was added in main.tex, after which 65 page images changed and all were viewed again; that pass showed a single-line spill at the top of page 34 (the last line of the BB1 gate quotation) and page 46 (the last line of the paragraph after the BB2 gate quotation). The BC2 sentence was reworded in uniform.tex and one extra line was allowed on the two quotation pages with \\enlargethispage in locality.tex and convergence.tex; no quoted gate text changed (token-exact comparison of all eight gates passed) and every page image that changed was viewed again. A SHA-256 comparison confirms that each of the 104 final page images is byte-identical to an image viewed after its last change. A final rebuild reproduced the same PDF, build receipt and page images byte for byte. The negation-aware phrase scan of all manuscript sources against the eight Round33 contracts returned no affirmative hit. Pre-merge scope corrections (2026-09-25, two passes after a read-only audit) changed main.tex, contributions.tex and applications.tex only: the abstract, the headline list of the status guide, three ledger rows (HNM-C-BC2, HNM-C-BD1, HNM-C-BD2) and two cells of Table 29 now carry the gate qualifiers (the BC1 certificates and padded-box sign at tau=+-10^-8, the AX2 node at tau=+10^-8 and s=1, the BD2 1x2 sign at l1=l2 on the grid with the D=8 width, the BD1 model scope, and SU(2) area parity at kappa=0 in centered whole-star boxes). The rebuilt PDF still has 104 pages. Every page was compared pixel by pixel (PIL ImageChops, empty difference bounding box) with the previously inspected full render: 93 pages are identical. The 11 changed pages (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 93, 101, 102, 103, 104) were rendered at 110 dpi and viewed one by one as images, across the two passes (a page changed only by the first pass was viewed then and is pixel-identical now). An overfull box introduced in the Table 29 two-plaquette cell by the first draft of the second pass was fixed before the final build; the final LaTeX log has no Overfull or Underfull box and no undefined reference, and no overflow, clipping, overlap or layout defect was found.",
  "schema": "hnm-round33-addendum-qa-v1",
  "scope": "Model-agent visual review plus automated geometry and reference diagnostics of the complete edition (BA1-BD2). Not human review; independent sample-page review is separate.",
  "status": "passed",
  "visual_findings": "Title, abstract and status and reading guide (pages 1-4), the model section with the obligations and plan tables (pages 5-10), the eight investigation sections BA1 to BD2 with their verbatim gate quotations and limitations (pages 11-91), the process history with the chronology and commit-order tables (pages 92-97), the limits section with the ranked roadmap (pages 98-100), the contribution and evidence ledger (pages 101-102) and the bibliography (pages 103-104), with headers, page numbers, equation tags, exact rationals, tables and displayed equations, are readable without clipping, overlap or overfull lines. Page 10 (Table 4) and page 93 (Table 29) are float-only pages, and pages 60-61 end short where the BC1 obligations longtable breaks before a tall row; these are accepted. Long exact rationals inside the ASCII gate quotations break across lines with no character added or removed. Some wide displays set their equation tag on the next line (for example equations (17), (30), (31) and (37)), which is the standard amsmath placement.",
  "visual_review": "passed"
